WEBVTT

00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:24,480
Any tips on PMR, not medical advice, but for an 83-year-old patient?

00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:34,080
Again, with PMR, you have to get to the cause of things.

00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:40,480
Like any disorder you have going on, you want to get to the cause of things.

00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:53,680
From a medical standpoint, with polymyalgia, any polymyalgia issues, they're typically just going to give you paid medication.

00:00:53,680 --> 00:01:00,280
From a functional standpoint, it's many times looked at as a chronic inflammation issue.

00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:07,880
Looking at blood work, you might find an increase in your inflammatory markers.

00:01:07,880 --> 00:01:15,080
Typically, blood work that's done on these type of people is just going to be a CVC in a complete metabolic panel.

00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:20,280
This is where I advocate highly into looking at autoimmune panels too.

00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:27,080
If you have antibodies to self-tissue, that's going to be a huge issue that you want to deal with.

00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:34,280
So digging into deeper blood work is going to be the key to that.

00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:37,480
That's really, honestly, the key to so many disorders.

00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:45,880
So many people are struggling with things that I hear are...

00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:48,680
I've been to multiple doctors, and I don't know how to treat this.

00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:56,280
Nobody's gotten to the bottom of this, and then you ask for that patient to send in all their labs.

00:01:56,280 --> 00:02:00,280
And it's amazing how few labs, many times, that people have,

00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:06,280
or all they've had done as a CVC in a complete metabolic panel through their GP.

00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:13,280
And sometimes it's really disturbing because sometimes they've even had gross abnormalities and that,

00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:16,280
and nothing was investigated and nothing was moved forward.

00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:21,080
Many times, people can have overwhelming symptoms because they have an ademia,

00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:24,280
but then nobody ever addresses the ademia.

00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:34,280
Back to another question on the Facebook page, any dietary changes for PMR.

00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:39,480
Just overall, there's some inflammatory process going on.

00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:43,880
So a person would do much better going on an anti-inflammatory diet.

00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:47,880
You could just Google an anti-inflammatory diet that would help.

00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:57,480
I would highly suspect, though, that there's specific dietary antibodies.

00:02:57,480 --> 00:03:03,480
Common with this would be gluten.

00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:11,080
Also, possibly lectins could be an issue because you could actually have rheumatoid factor positive.

00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:15,080
That would be the benefit of doing an antibody test.

00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:24,280
And then if R.A. is antibodies are present, then I would say lectins can be a big culprit.

00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:29,080
So you could look up a lectin, a low lectin diet or a lectin-free diet,

00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:34,680
certainly gluten-free diet and just overall just an anti-inflammatory diet.

00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:40,680
And like anything, when you have an uptick of inflammation, systemic inflammation in the body,

00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:43,480
you always have to think that there's inflammation in the gut.

00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:47,880
That's why food sensitivity panels, like a Cyrexarate 10,

00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:54,280
would be the right choice in something like this because it's amazing what you could do

00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:59,080
when you calm down the gut, what you could do from a systemic standpoint.

00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:02,680
I've had people with inflammatory arithritis, you know,

00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:06,280
they were diagnosed with psoriatic arthritis or rheumatoid arthritis.

00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:10,680
It would just clean up the gut and did a Cyrexarate 10,

00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:14,600
cleaned up the gut with diets, things that are causing inflammation that got

00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:20,680
all their symptoms calm down. Now, the longer you have an arthritis like that,

00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:24,040
you have bony changes. We're never going to change those bony changes,

00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:30,520
but if you could decrease the inflammation, you could decrease, you know, 95% of the patient's symptoms.

00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:37,640
So like anything, you're always looking for the cause. You're always looking for the source.

00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:42,040
So you're going to be digging to that source and, you know,

00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,280
it's not enough to say, oh, you have inflammation.

00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:48,200
Your C-reactor protein is high, your hybridid is high.

00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:54,120
You know, something like that, you want to go, okay, well, why is that?

00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,440
You know, what is the cause of that as well?

00:04:56,440 --> 00:05:00,440
So digging to that is important.

